#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Nuxel pre-lockscreen cinema controller (PWNAGE-31000).

The controller is deliberately a *presentation overlay*, not a service manager:
it never starts, stops, fakes or waits for application services.  It starts the
already-installed ``mpv`` as a fullscreen, audio-free Wayland client after the
compositor and the ``nuxel-wl-fb`` display bridge are up, keeps the real Nuxel
lockscreen alive underneath, and releases the overlay only when:

  * the video has reached EOF (or the bounded display interval has paused it), and
  * the real lockscreen has published its readiness receipt,
  * the display bridge is still healthy and the panel is on, and
  * the touch path has settled (ARMED_OK, or an honest NO_TOUCH_DEVICE warning).

Every failure path is fail-open: the overlay exits and the existing lockscreen /
fallback remains.  The controller never calls ``unlock``, never writes a display
surface, and never owns ``/dev/fb0``.  The running ``nuxel-wl-fb`` remains the
single framebuffer owner.

Why mpv and not WebKit's <video> on this handset
------------------------------------------------
The deployed WebKitGTK 2.52 host deliberately disables media when
``libgstautodetect.so`` is absent (measured A29b: ``autoaudiosink`` missing
aborts WebKitWebProcess).  ``mpv`` 0.40 + FFmpeg 7.1 is installed, decodes the
existing H.264 High 1080x1920 asset in software, and exposes ``vo=wlshm`` (a
real Wayland SHM client), so it needs no new package or DRM/EGL path.

This file is stdlib-only.  It is exercised offline by
tests/pwnage31000/test_preload_cinema.py with a fake mpv/IPC peer.
"""

